# A path write after a call with an effect, through an alias declared BEFORE the call. A route that cannot prove the
# alias target after the call takes the whole callable through the walker; it must not run `main` natively up to the
# write and then replay it, and the preparation must not run `touch`. touch counts its runs: `seen := seen + 1`. One
# evaluation gives seen 1; a prepared or partly started native body replayed by the walker would give seen 2. done 9 is
# the write after the call. Every route answers the same (the book, #frame-and-graph-assignment). The form uses no write
# of a caller's alias by a callee through a hidden binding: that is the separate M14 debt, not pinned here.
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
        int: done 0
)
sub: touch ()
    @: shared node[0]
    shared\Observed\seen := shared\Observed\seen + 1
sub: main ()
    @: shared node[0]
    touch()
    shared\Observed\done := 9
main()
